<title>DUBAI: GCC to meet on bank branches in member states.</title>
<headline>GCC to meet on bank branches in member states.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1996-11-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Gulf Cooperation Council (GCC) committee will meet in Riyadh on Monday to discuss the basis for allowing regional banks to open branches in member states, the six-nation alliance said on Sunday.</p>
<p>The technical meeting follows the endorsement in principle of the idea by GCC central bank governors at their meeting in Bahrain last month, it added in a statement.</p>
<p>The GCC -- Saudi Arabia, Kuwait, United Arab Emirates, Qatar, Oman and Bahrain -- a political, economic and military alliance, is working on unifying economic and monetary policies as part of a plan to set up a regional market.</p>
</text>
